  m_Name: 6.Court House
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  nameOfPoint: Court House
  coordinatesPoint: {x: 14.51214, y: 35.89923}
  firstPartInfo: "The police found that there was enough <link=Image_6a><u><color=blue>material</link></u></color>to
    charge Isidoro Mifsud before the court. When it was time for his case to be heard
    before a judge, he would have been brought here. In the 1850s, the criminal court
    was moved to the Auberge d\u2019Auvergne, which used to stand in this location. 
    During the Second World War, the building was hit and the courts were moved,
    till 1971, when they were re-housed in the building you see before you. "
  secondPartInfo: "The jury (8 out of 9) delivered a verdict of \u2018guilty\u2019.
    They recommended that his previous good conduct and his young age be taken into
    account. The sentence was 18 months\u2019 hard labour. Unfortunately, the archive
    trail ends here, and we do not know the outcome of the case or the punishment
    meted out. The volume that would have contained the court case files for that
    year is missing.  This is not uncommon: when doing archival work, people and
    their stories often disappear into gaps in the record. In following the trails
    of Isidoro Mifsud and Teresa Dimech, I have caught a glimpse of the terrible
    poverty that much of the Maltese population suffered at the time - a poverty
    whose widespread extent and visibility may be difficult to imagine now, but one
    that still haunts our history.    I have also seen a relationship between poverty
    and the law, where the desperation of poverty might have pushed some to crime
    out of necessity; yet in its zeal to look out for property rights, the law also
    sometimes contributed to worsening (sometimes even criminalising) the conditions
    of those who were under-privileged. Law protects, but not always equally."
  imgMarker: {fileID: 21300000, guid: c98feaebd40d8df449e6d3855ac84352, type: 3}
  imgMain: {fileID: 21300000, guid: f26fa8880b3aeef4b8516c82dc12f2a5, type: 3}
  nameOfStory: Poverty
